  "description": "arbitration.v1 §2.4: a binding (its entries in their configured order, each <system>/<service>, a chunk possibly *) and the addresses heard -> the providers in rank order. An entry matches an address when each of its chunks is * or equal to the address's. An address ranks at the first entry that matches it; addresses at one entry are ordered by system, then by service, each compared byte by byte (never the text <system>/<service> whole). expect.ranked: every exact entry's address (heard or not) and every heard address some entry matches, once each, in rank order; expect.unbound: the heard addresses no entry matches, ordered by system then service, once each; expect.wildcards: the 0-based positions of the entries with a * chunk; expect.shadowed: the 0-based positions of the entries that can rank no address of their own, an entry at position j being shadowed when an earlier entry i < j matches every address it does (each chunk of i is * or equal to j's)."
